# runmarq needs no environment variables to run locally. Everything below is optional.

# --- Desktop app and CLI ---------------------------------------------------
# Use a different data directory (tests, portable setups).
# RUNMARQ_HOME=/path/to/runmarq-data
# Log level for the collector and desktop app: error, warn, info, debug, trace.
# RUNMARQ_LOG=info
# Write each raw hook payload to this folder, for building test fixtures.
# Captures contain prompts and tool input: review before sharing.
# RUNMARQ_CAPTURE_DIR=/path/to/captures

# --- Website (apps/web) -----------------------------------------------------
# All website settings are read at build time; set them in the hosting
# provider's environment variables and redeploy after changing one.
# The public address, used for the sitemap, robots.txt, llms.txt and link
# previews. On Vercel it defaults to the production domain.
# SITE_URL=https://runmarq.example
# Shown in the header, footer and contact page when set.
# GITHUB_URL=https://github.com/owner/runmarq
# CONTACT_EMAIL=hello@runmarq.example
# Enables the early-access form. Sign-ups are POSTed as JSON
# {email, platform, consentedAt, source} to this HTTPS endpoint, which must
# store them durably and return 409 for an address it already has.
# Leave unset to show the honest "not open yet" state.
# EARLY_ACCESS_WEBHOOK_URL=https://example.com/hooks/early-access
# Sent as "Authorization: Bearer <secret>" to the endpoint above.
# EARLY_ACCESS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
